1. Start.
2. Create three linked lists P1, P2 and P3 for the two input polynomials and the result.
3. Read the number of terms of P1.
4. Read the coefficient and exponent of each term and insert them into P1 in descending order of exponent.
5. Read the number of terms of P2.
6. Read the coefficient and exponent of each term and insert them into P2 in descending order of exponent.
7. Set pointers to the first nodes of P1 and P2.
8. Compare the exponents of the current nodes.
9. If the exponents are equal:
      Add the coefficients and insert the sum into P3.
      Move both pointers to the next nodes.
10. If the exponent of P1 is greater:
      Copy the term of P1 into P3.
      Move the P1 pointer to the next node.
11. Otherwise:
      Copy the term of P2 into P3.
      Move the P2 pointer to the next node.
12. Repeat steps 8 to 11 until either P1 or P2 becomes NULL.
13. Copy all remaining terms of P1 or P2 into P3.
14. Display P1, P2 and P3.
15. Free all allocated memory.
16. Stop.
